# ── 2026-09-30 (333-AGI): human intake data must not be swept into a PUBLIC repo ──
# This repository's GitHub remote is PUBLIC (measured: visibility=PUBLIC).
# intake/processed/*.json records now carry `signals.quote` — a VERBATIM sovereign
# utterance from a Telegram DM, tagged evidence_class=SOVEREIGN_VERBAL_SELF_REPORT.
# The previously tracked intake/processed/voice-2026-09-07*.json has NO quote field,
# so committing the new one would have been the first verbatim personal quote
# published here — permanently, since removal needs a history rewrite and forks or
# caches may already hold it. F6 MARUAH / F4: excluded, not published.
# Quarantine is by definition withheld-from-circulation content (this batch includes
# REDACTED-VERSE and an item flagged `laundered-as-self-report`), so it must never
# be committed at all. Already-tracked files stay tracked; gitignore does not untrack.
# DURABLE FIX (organ owner, not a gitignore): redact or hash `signals.quote` at
# write time, or move intake records out of the repo tree entirely.
intake/_quarantine*/
intake/processed/*.json
# gitignore is inert on already-tracked paths — the four human-data records below
# were tracked before this rule existed and are now `git rm --cached` (2026-09-30).
state.json.*

# machine-written deploy stamps — rewritten by scripts/refresh_deploy_stamp.sh on every
# boot (well.service.d/p0-stamp-refresh.conf ExecStartPre). Never committable.
.git_commit
release-manifest.json
